; dfs90sel
;
; TS3 / 06.07.2011
;
; double frequency sweep followed by a selective excitation pulse
; this pulse program can be used to selectively invert satellites of spin = n/2 
; nuclei for signal enhancement
; to optimise a sweep for further use in MQMAS, set duration of sweep to 1/4 of a 
; rotor period, and width of sweep to about 1 MHz, then optimise RF power 
; starting at low amplitude and increase up to below RF power of excitation pulse
; use the value found for the maximum signal in mp3qdfs or mp3qdfsz for further refinement
; use aunm:zg_dfs to calculate the dfs shape
;
;Avance III
;parameters:
;pl1 : = 0W, not used
;pl21 : power level for selective 90 degree pulse
;sp1 : power for frequency sweep
;p2 : duration of sweep
;p3 : 90 degree pulse, selective, at plw21
;p25 : dummy pulse, used for calculations only
;d1 : recycle delay
;d4 : short delay between sweep and read out pulse
;ns : 2 * n
;spnam1 : dfs
;cnst1 : (in kHz) Startfrequency of sweep
;cnst2 : (in kHz) Endfrequency of sweep
;cnst3 : (in ns) timing resolution of sweep, down to 25 ns
;cnst31 : spinning frequency
;cnst0 : to define sweep as fraction or multiples of rotor period
;
;
;$CLASS=Solids
;$DIM=1D
;$TYPE=half integer quadrupoles
;$SUBTYPE=simple 1D
;$COMMENT=selective CT excitation with double frequency sweep (DFS) enhancement

prosol relations=<solids_mqmas>


"p25=(1u*cnst1/(cnst3+cnst2))+1u"
"p2=1s/(cnst31*cnst0)"
"acqt0=0"

1 ze
2 d1
  (p2:sp1 ph1):f1
  d4
  (p3 pl21 ph2):f1
  go=2 ph31
  wr #0 
exit

ph1= 0 2 1 3
ph2= 0 2 1 3
ph31=0 2 1 3



;$Id:$
